      "message": "feat(app): work offsets post as an index bounded by the setup's own post\n\nSlice 2 of #931. The stream carries the setup's 1-based offset index\n(Dump::wcs is a u32; posting::wcs_context returns the index). The\nsix-offset cap leaves core: SetSetupWorkOffset checks the pick against\nthe setup's own post, a new verification clause\n(setup_offsets::range_problems) refuses by setup name an offset the\nsetup's post cannot express, and the loader keeps only the u8 sanity\nbound. A stored offset is never read as offset 1 anywhere - not in\nsetup::work_offset, wcs_context, the label or the setup sheet.\n\nsetup::work_offset_names reads the post's name table (cached per post\nand script text) for labels, the setup sheet and refusal texts; display\nonly. Offsets 1-6 still save as G54..G59 (byte-identical files); 7+\nsave as their number, which older builds cannot open. WCS_SLOTS becomes\nthe crate-private legacy entity-name list.\n\nRefs #931\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
